   cd berkeley_upc-2022.10.0
   ./configure --prefix=/usr/local --disable-mpi --enable-smp --disable-ibv --disable-shmem --disable-ofi --disable-ucx
   make && make install
   export PATH=/usr/local/upc/bin:$PATH
   ```

2. Build and run:
   ```
   cd /app && make pgen
   upcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB /app/pgen test
   ```

3. Verify correctness:
   ```
   sort serial.out > /tmp/serial_sorted.txt
   cat pgen_*.out | sort > /tmp/pgen_sorted.txt
   diff /tmp/serial_sorted.txt /tmp/pgen_sorted.txt
   ```

**Key design of the parallel version (`pgen.c`):**
- The hash table is shared across all threads (SMP mode)
- Each thread processes hash buckets where `bucket_index % THREADS == MYTHREAD`
- Per-bucket locks (`upc_lock_t`) protect the `visited` flag during traversal
- Thread 0 reads the input file and builds the hash table; all threads participate in traversal
- Each thread writes its contigs to `pgen_<thread_id>.out`
- Thread 0 handles cleanup of the hash table

